the knowledge base or_example includes:

the text of the source program is at "sources/or-example.l4".

gets discount if
    is student
    or is senior.

any true for a boolean with a second boolean with a third boolean if
    true is equal to the boolean
    or true is equal to the second boolean
    or true is equal to the third boolean.

has access if
    is admin
    or is owner
    or has permission.

is terminal a status if
    "completed" is equal to the status
    or "cancelled" is equal to the status
    or "failed" is equal to the status.

the get priority for an user type with a boolean is a text if
    "admin" is equal to the user type
    or true is equal to the boolean
    and the text is equal to "high"
    otherwise the text is equal to "normal".

complex condition for a number N with a boolean if
    N > 0
    and N < 100
    or true is equal to the boolean.

